  "content": {
    "id": "p42-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Solve in the domain $x\\in[-\\pi,\\pi]$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p42-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\cos^2x=\\sqrt3\\sin x\\cos x$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac{5\\pi}{6},-\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
          "worked": "For $\\cos x\\ne0$, divide by $\\cos x$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos x&=\\sqrt3\\sin x\\\\\\tan x&=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}\\\\x&=\\frac\\pi6,-\\frac{5\\pi}6\\end{align*}$$\n\nCheck $\\cos x=0$: $x=\\pm\\frac\\pi2$.\n\nAt $x=\\frac\\pi2$:\n$$0=\\sqrt3(1)(0)\\quad\\checkmark$$\n\nAt $x=-\\frac\\pi2$:\n$$0=\\sqrt3(-1)(0)\\quad\\checkmark$$\n\nTherefore\n$$x=-\\frac{5\\pi}{6},-\\frac\\pi2,\\frac\\pi6,\\frac\\pi2.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
      },
      {
        "id": "p42-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\cos^2x-\\sin^2x=3\\sin x-1$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac\\pi6,\\frac{5\\pi}6$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}1-\\sin^2x-\\sin^2x&=3\\sin x-1\\\\2\\sin^2x+3\\sin x-2&=0\\\\(2\\sin x-1)(\\sin x+2)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $\\sin x=\\frac12$ or $\\sin x=-2$.\n\nReject $\\sin x=-2$, since $-1\\le\\sin x\\le1$.\n\nOn $[-\\pi,\\pi]$:\n$$x=\\frac\\pi6,\\frac{5\\pi}6.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
  },
